# THE GATE TOOLCHAIN, PINNED ONCE.
#
# Every tool a CI gate shells out to is versioned here and nowhere else, so the
# same gate reaches the same verdict on a developer's host, inside the devbox,
# and on a CI runner. Before this file existed they did not: measured 2026-08-25
# on one machine, the host had node v24.14.0 / go1.25.13 / shellcheck 0.9.0 while
# the container had node v22.23.2 / go1.26.4 / no shellcheck at all, and CI had a
# third combination again. shfmt was installed twice from two unpinned sources
# that agreed only by luck.
#
# FORMAT IS LOAD-BEARING: plain KEY=value, no quotes, no $, no spaces, no
# `readonly`. That is the intersection of what three different readers accept,
# which is what lets one file be the only copy:
#
#   bash      set -a; . .devcontainer/toolchain.env; set +a   (via .ci/config/constants.sh)
#   Docker    COPY toolchain.env /etc/rediacc/ + ARG          (a Dockerfile cannot source bash)
#   Actions   cat .devcontainer/toolchain.env >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
#
# WHY IT LIVES HERE and not in .ci/config/: the devcontainer image build context
# IS .devcontainer/ (.github/workflows/ci-build-docker.yml:558, .ci/lib/devbox.sh:263).
# COPY cannot reach outside the context, and widening the context to the repo
# root would upload the entire tree plus submodules on every image build.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE, stated so nobody "completes" the file:
#   * npm/pip dependency versions -- package-lock.json and the lockfiles own those.
#     eslint, biome, playwright and tsx are already single-sourced there.
#   * NFPM_VERSION and the SHA256 constants (.ci/config/constants.sh:149-166).
#     Those are PACKAGING pins; the image build has no use for them.
# The rule is "a version a GATE depends on, that more than one lane installs".

# Linters and formatters the gates invoke.
RUFF_VERSION=0.16.1
SHFMT_VERSION=3.13.1
SHELLCHECK_VERSION=0.10.0
ACTIONLINT_VERSION=1.7.12
PYYAML_VERSION=6.0.2

# Language runtimes. NODE_VERSION is the major CI installs
# (.github/actions/setup-workspace/action.yml:21); GO_VERSION is what the image
# provides. Note that private/renet/go.mod carries its own `toolchain` directive:
# these are deliberately separate numbers, because go.mod pins what renet is
# COMPILED WITH and this pins what the image SHIPS.
NODE_VERSION=22
GO_VERSION=1.26.4
